# Function power (D-7): a superscript on a function name applies the
# function that many times; `f_^0` is the identity. A quoted function
# may carry one (`'u:d_ouble^3`).
== SOURCE
n_eg^3 5
r_ev^2 1 2 3
n_eg^0 5
u:d_ouble := { _r * 2 }
u:d_ouble^10 1
'u:d_ouble^3 e_ach 1 2
== TYPE
Int
Int
Int
u:d_ouble : Num a => a -> a
Int
Int
== RESULT
